# Stripe Environment Protection Contract

Full reference: `docs/guardrails/2026-07-23_stripe-environment-protection-contract.md`

## Hard rule (PRODUCTION SAFETY)

**Menuply production must remain on Stripe live mode at all times.**

No agent may switch production (website, backend, DB, webhooks, or env vars) to Stripe sandbox/test mode unless Andre Barber’s **current-turn** message grants explicit temporary permission for that specific task.

Silence, implied approval, prior approval, debugging convenience, or agent judgment ≠ permission.

## Preferred testing (always)

Local test keys · preview/staging · Stripe CLI forwarding · mocks · automated tests that do **not** alter production config.

## Never without Andre’s explicit temporary-sandbox permission

- Overwrite production live keys with test keys
- Point production webhooks at test endpoints
- Deploy code that defaults production to test mode
- Fall back to test credentials when live config is missing (fail closed instead)
- Leave production in test mode after testing or on handoff

## Agent stop condition

If production sandbox seems necessary without permission, stop and report:

> This task appears to require temporarily changing production Stripe configuration. I have not made that change because explicit authorization is required. I will use local, preview, staging, mocked, or Stripe CLI testing instead.

## Before editing production Stripe / payment env

Output:

> **Per Stripe Environment Protection Contract: the proposed change will modify [names] and may alter production Stripe live/sandbox mode. Explicit Andre authorization required.**

Then stop until approved.

## If temporary sandbox is authorized

Warn continuously: **PRODUCTION STRIPE IS TEMPORARILY IN TEST MODE — RESTORATION REQUIRED**  
Restore and verify live mode before declaring done. Required statement:

> Stripe production configuration has been restored and independently verified as live. No temporary sandbox configuration remains active.

## Mandatory on every task completion

End every response with:

> ☐ STRIPE ENVIRONMENT CERTIFICATION: Production Stripe [unchanged live | restored+verified live | Andre-authorized temporary sandbox — restoration pending].

Do not expose Stripe secret values in logs, chat, docs, or commits.
